{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/861870-mtr-has-a-death-rebirth-cycle","id":861870,"title":"MtR has a Death/Rebirth cycle?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-04-08T08:58:30-07:00","id":861870,"title":"MtR has a Death/Rebirth cycle?","content":"It's an information I cannot find anywere. I know that a mummy come back to life after a cooldown time if she get killed. But I were whondering if mummies have also a death/rebirth cycle similar to Mummy the Curse as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2457-ipergigio","name":"Ipergigio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2457_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-09T02:43:30-07:00","id":862533,"title":"","content":"Most mummies don't. When one is ready to return from the Underworld, they literally bring their corpse back to life, pouring &quot;Ba&quot; energies in to repair any damage or rotting that may have occurred. No matter how badly injured that body may have been - even if ground into a fine power and digested - the mummy can restore it good as new. Nor is old age a factor - growing &quot;old&quot; for a mummy is more about their batteries (so to speak) running down, rather than going grey.<br /> <br /> I think that changed for the Egyptian mummies, though, who went through the revised rites that the revived Osiris brought back from the Underworld. Unfortunately, I don't have the last edition of <b>Mummy</b> myself, but if memory serves, the participating mummies did get a rebirth/reincarnation element. However, the Cabiri, Bane Mummies, &quot;Others&quot;, and any Egyptian mummy who <i>didn't</i> undergo the new rite stayed with the old system of resurrecting their corpse. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","name":"One Vorlon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"537"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-09T04:03:55-07:00","id":862542,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ipergigio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/861870-mtr-has-a-death-rebirth-cycle#post861870\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's an information I cannot find anywere. I know that a mummy come back to life after a cooldown time if she get killed. But I were whondering if mummies have also a death/rebirth cycle similar to Mummy the Curse as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Ba background in the MTR corebook, page 64. By default, the Reborn have an average 60-year lifespan, with dots in Ba extending it up to 110 years; however, they don't age, suffer the effects of aging, or undergo any loss in power (their power is tied to Balance, their Morality trait).<br /> <br /> Ba also determines how long they need to stay in the Underworld (although they can choose to stay longer); a year by default, which Ba can reduce down to a day.<br /> <br /> There's no real emphasis on the cycle, as there is with MTC, as it's not what Resurrection's concerned with","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-09T09:26:41-07:00","id":862616,"title":"","content":"Time in Duat seemed more like a debrief and some R&amp;R than anything else. Until the whole storm thing....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-09T17:02:36-07:00","id":862862,"title":"","content":"So Resurrection's mummies can stay &quot;operative&quot; for 60 years and do not age? For sure Curse's mummies must be very jealous! ^^;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2457,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2457-ipergigio","user":"Ipergigio","date":". 04-09-2016, 08:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2457-ipergigio","name":"Ipergigio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2457_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-09T19:19:15-07:00","id":862957,"title":"","content":"And they can rearrange the weather in, say, a hemisphere....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars